//! Shared application simulation: source orchestration for every game family.
//!
//! Port of `/home/buzzkill/Projects/quake-typescript/src/app/bootstrap/simulation/runtime.ts`
//! (`SharedSimulation`, `createSimulation`, `orderedActorTurns`, `loadSimulation`).
//!
//! Missing siblings (no Rust home in this worktree; mirrored below, unify post-merge):
//! `players.ts` ([`MovementPlayer`], `movementOrigin`, `movementVelocity`,
//! `movementProfile`, `providerFamily`, `providerTiming`), `bots.ts`
//! ([`SimulationBotServices`]), `bot-mover-connections.ts`
//! (`applicationTrainConnections`), `bot-prediction.ts`
//! (`predictApplicationBotMovement`), `../content.ts`
//! (`LoadedApplicationContent`, only behind seams), and
//! `../weapon-behavior-selection.ts` (`PreparedWeaponBehavior` selection,
//! already mirrored as [`PreparedWeaponBehavior`](super::types::PreparedWeaponBehavior)).
//!
//! Structural divergences from the donor, all forced by Rust ownership:
//!
//! * [`SharedSimulation`] is a cheap cloneable handle over
//!   `Rc<RefCell<SharedSimulationState>>`. Every donor method takes `&self`
//!   and borrows the state in narrow scopes: never hold a state borrow
//!   across a call into physics, events, combat, scheduler, scene, sources,
//!   or weapon behaviors, because those subsystems call back into the state
//!   through the stored [`Weak`] handles. Re-entrant `borrow_mut` panics are
//!   a port bug, not a runtime condition.
//! * Donor `async` load boundaries are sync and take
//!   `next_frame: &mut dyn FnMut()`, matching the
//!   `weapon-behavior-runtime` precedent.
//! * `Map<OwnedActor, _>` keys stay `OwnedActor` (`Hash` was added to
//!   `qa_core::identity::OwnedActor` for this port).
//! * Donor closures stored on the instance (physics/combat/scheduler/event
//!   options, mod-client services, release listeners) become either stored
//!   `Weak` handles upgraded inside small free functions, or plain methods.
//!   [`ModClientServices`] keeps its donor data (`maximum`) while its donor
//!   closures live as `SharedSimulation` methods.
//! * `SourceRuntime` variants that alias live subsystem objects in the donor
//!   (Q2 flattened product views, round settlement) resolve through the
//!   state instead of holding second references.

